  evidence:
  - evidence_type: RECIPE_SOURCE
    source: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=317
    source_record: JCM 317 Se/W solution; complete named stock table and preparation
      notes
    notes: The JCM317 dihydrate is explicit; a difference from NBRC1020 is not established
      by its omitted hydrate qualifier. The previously recorded comparisons with JCM852
      lower amounts/hydrated selenite and JCM431 alkaline formula are retained. NBRC1020
      prints Na2SeO3 4 mg and Na2WO4 4 mg with 1 L distilled water; the missing hydrate
      qualifiers do not establish anhydrous reagents. JCM317 explicitly prints Na2WO4·2H2O
      4 mg with Na2SeO3 4 mg and 1 L distilled water. The shared nominal amounts and
      omitted NBRC hydrate do not establish either identical or distinct supplied
      preparations. Retain both source-bound partial proposals without merging or
      co-installing them as proved-distinct owners until supplied-form/applicability
      evidence or an explicitly reviewed common nominal scope resolves the overlap.
      The water amounts are added-water batch quantities, not instructions to make
      up a final litre. Literal printed masses and added distilled-water volume per
      source preparation. G/MG_PER_PREPARATION_WITH_1_L_WATER describes a recipe batch
      containing1L added water, not a final1L solution or final concentration.
